{
  "summary": "This multimodal experiment (single profile, scvi_n200, ResNet50, concat) achieved a validation accuracy of 0.536 (F1: 0.516), a ~0.9-point improvement over the otherwise identical PCA n2000 configuration (0.527, F1: 0.510; llm_summary_002), confirming that the scvi encoder advantage seen in the RNA-only setting (~3.5 pts, llm_summary_004) persists in the multimodal context, albeit at a reduced magnitude. This establishes scvi_n200 as the preferred RNA encoder for subsequent multimodal and multiprofile experiments. It remains uncertain whether the attenuated gain reflects partial redundancy between the learned nonlinear latent and image features under concat fusion, whether alternative fusion strategies or multiprofile settings could further widen the encoder gap, and whether the result is stable across random initializations."
}

